  "_meta": {
    "table": "nutra_botanicals",
    "version": "0.1",
    "purpose": "D-139: the plants in Schedule II of the FSS (Nutra) Regulations 2022 whose row carries a note a user would read (pregnancy, children, conception, diabetics, prolonged use...). A supplement listing one gets a tile quoting the note exactly, with the part.",
    "source": {
      "title": "FSS (Health Supplements, Nutraceuticals, Food for Special Dietary Use, Food for Special Medical Purpose and Prebiotic and Probiotic Food) Regulations, 2022, Annexure 2, Schedule II, as operationalised by FSSAI's direction of 18 October 2022",
      "url": "https://fssai.gov.in/docs/food-law/regulations/Direction_New_compressed.pdf",
      "pages": "Annexure pp. 23 to 55 (PDF pp. 26 to 58)",
      "read_on": "2026-09-30"
    },
    "rules": [
      "Every row was copied from the page image (the PDF's text layer merges cells at page breaks), all 33 pages read. Rows without a note are not here: the schedule says nothing a user would read about them beyond the usage range.",
      "The note is quoted exactly as printed, spelling included (row 370: \"recommdeded\", \"beow\").",
      "Names are the schedule's own (its Latin names and its \"Official and common names\" column). A name printed on two rows is left out: \"Sage\" (rows 363 and 427), \"Saral\" (rows 312 and 314). No other English names (D-139).",
      "A note belongs to a part. When the plant has other parts in the schedule, the tile shows only if the pack's entry names the noted part (parts_in_schedule). `placement` marks a note the schedule doesn't box to one part.",
      "Schedule II Notes 4 and 5 (p. 55): the usage range for children 5 to 16 years is half the adult range, 2 to 5 years a quarter."
    ],
    "who_values": "pregnancy | under_5 | under_16 | conceiving | lactating | children | diabetes | condition | all"
  },
